# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The Dockerfile only copies `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock`, `src` and `.streamlit`,
# so nothing here is required by a build -- but the context is transferred to the
# daemon in full before that COPY happens. Without this file every build ships
# `.venv` (1.4GB), `data/` (163MB) and `.git` across, and `.secrets/` / `.env`
# would land in the image the moment anyone writes a broader COPY.

# --- Secrets: never in the build context ---
.secrets/
.env
.env.*
**/.env

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
**/.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/

# --- Version control & CI ---
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- Editor / container / agent tooling ---
.vscode
.devcontainer
.claude
.mcp.json
.zed

# --- Docker itself ---
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
compose.yaml
**/compose.yaml
**/docker-compose.yml

# --- Data: fixtures and the local lake are not part of any image ---
data/

# --- Local Iceberg catalog (SQLite) ---
configuration/iceberg/catalog/

# --- dbt build artifacts ---
**/target/
**/dbt_packages/
**/logs/

# --- Notebooks and prototypes ---
src/Jupyter/
**/*.ipynb
**/.ipynb_checkpoints

# --- Python bytecode / build output ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/*.so
build/
dist/
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.egg

# --- Test & coverage artifacts ---
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.nox/
**/.tox/
tests/

# --- Logs ---
**/*.log

# --- Docs & repo meta ---
docs/
git/
README.md
LICENSE

# --- Tool configuration not needed at runtime ---
.pre-commit-config.yaml
ruff.toml
pyrightconfig.json
.python-version
